PRE-REGISTRATION -- does DESCRIPTION FIDELITY replicate on coach?   2026-09-12
Written at 11:24, BEFORE any coach per-skill data exists. The coach FULL arm ran
once (58.3%, 2026-09-12 ~10:27) but persisted only aggregates; per-skill scores
have never been seen.

WHY REPLICATE
  The fidelity finding (rho +0.637 coverage-vs-accuracy, 50-point tertile spread)
  rests on ONE catalogue, ayoai-mind's 140 skills. Two catalogues is not
  "generalizes" -- it is "did not break on the second one" -- but one catalogue is
  a single observation, and the arc has already retired three drivers that looked
  solid on one catalogue.

CONSTRAINTS (unchanged from the ADR-0155 coach run)
  Coach's skill text never leaves zc-03. The script runs ON the box, stdlib only,
  and prints correlations, tertile means and counts -- never a description, a
  query, or a skill name. Coverage is computed on-box from the same tokenizer BM25
  uses. Pod credentials come from /etc/zakcode/.env via _dotenv(), never printed.

CO-TENANCY, stated because the last run repeated the lesson
  The TOPK eval holds the pod (shortlist arms, ~7s/query). Coach FULL is 192
  prefix-cached queries at ~1s each -- a 3-4 minute burst. It costs TOPK latency,
  not correctness: the provider reproduces 5/5 byte-identically at temp 0 under
  load (probe_provider_determinism.py), and the determinism load control
  reproduced IDENTICAL under this same TOPK load. Accepted and recorded.

MEASURE (identical to description_fidelity.py, ported to stdlib)
  Per skill: mean over its 3 queries of (query tokens present in name+description)
  / (query tokens), same tokenizer as BM25. Outcome: FULL-catalogue accuracy per
  skill, re-run now with per-skill persistence. Sanity: BM25 recall@20 per skill.

PREDICTIONS, fixed before data
  C0 FULL reproduces: within 5 points of the prior 58.3%. VOID below 45%.
  C1 (sanity) coverage vs BM25 recall@20: rho >= +0.15. Near-tautological; if it
     fails the on-box coverage port is broken and NOTHING else counts.
  C2 (the test) coverage vs FULL accuracy: rho >= +0.15, positive.
  C3 tertile spread (highest-third FULL accuracy minus lowest-third) >= 25 points
     -- half the 50 observed on ayoai-mind, a boundary strictly inside the
     predicted direction (guard-5645), not at the observed value.
  C4 F3 holds again: rho(C2) < rho(C1) -- the model is less lexical than BM25.

DECISION RULES
  C0 fails -> the arm drifted or the instrument broke; no verdict on anything.
  C1 fails -> coverage port broken; no verdict on C2-C4.
  C2 AND C3 hold -> fidelity REPLICATES on an independent catalogue. The ADR may
     say "on both catalogues measured", never "generalizes".
  C2 holds, C3 fails -> replicates in DIRECTION, weaker in magnitude. Report both
     numbers; the ayoai-mind spread does not transfer as a magnitude.
  C2 fails -> DOES NOT REPLICATE. The fidelity finding is SCOPED to ayoai-mind's
     catalogue, and that scoping goes in the ADR headline, not a footnote. Do not
     rescue it by changing the coverage measure until one correlates.

WHAT THIS CANNOT DO
  64 skills, 192 queries. A correlation on n=64 has wide uncertainty; no CI is
  computed for rho and none will be quoted. Still no causal claim -- only a
  rewrite arm separates "low coverage causes failure" from "low coverage marks
  ambiguous skills".
